{
  "conversation_lines": [
    {
      "turn_number": 1,
      "time": "2172-02-24 12:15:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Hi, I'm Dr. Lee. I’ll be taking care of you during your stay. Can you tell me what happened?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 2,
      "time": "2172-02-24 12:16:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "I fell off my chair at home. I twisted my ankle and heard a pop. It hurt right away and swelled up."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 3,
      "time": "2172-02-24 12:17:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Did you feel dizzy or pass out before the fall?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 4,
      "time": "2172-02-24 12:18:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "No, I didn’t. It was just a mechanical fall. I was trying to get up and lost my balance."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 5,
      "time": "2172-02-24 12:19:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Okay. The X-ray shows a fracture in your lower tibia, but the ankle joint looks intact. No surgery is needed, but you’ll need to keep it immobilized."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 6,
      "time": "2172-02-24 12:20:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "So I won’t need surgery? That’s good. But walking is out of the question, right?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 7,
      "time": "2172-02-24 12:21:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Exactly. You’ll be on crutches or a walker. We’ll arrange physical therapy and possibly rehab to help you regain strength."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 8,
      "time": "2172-02-24 12:22:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "I don’t know about rehab. I just want to go home."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 9,
      "time": "2172-02-24 12:23:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "I understand, but with your medical history, we want to make sure you’re safe. We also noticed something else—your INR was very high, at 7.5."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 10,
      "time": "2172-02-24 12:24:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "INR? That’s from my Coumadin, right? I’ve been on it for years."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 11,
      "time": "2172-02-24 12:25:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Yes. A normal INR is around 2 to 3 for someone on Coumadin. Yours was dangerously high, which increases bleeding risk. We’ve held the Coumadin for now."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 12,
      "time": "2172-02-24 12:26:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Oh. Should I be worried about bleeding?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 13,
      "time": "2172-02-24 12:27:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "We’re monitoring closely. No signs of bleeding now. We’ll restart Coumadin at a lower dose once your INR comes down."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 14,
      "time": "2172-02-24 12:28:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Okay, that makes sense."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 15,
      "time": "2172-02-24 12:29:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "You also mentioned shortness of breath when lying flat. Is that new?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 16,
      "time": "2172-02-24 12:30:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "No, it’s been going on for a while. I think my legs are more swollen than usual too."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 17,
      "time": "2172-02-24 12:31:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Your chest X-ray shows signs of fluid buildup, likely from your heart failure. We’ll give you some diuretics to help with that."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 18,
      "time": "2172-02-24 12:32:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "I’m already on Lasix. Is that not enough?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 19,
      "time": "2172-02-24 12:33:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "You were on 40 mg twice daily. We’ll keep that for now and monitor your weight and symptoms. We want to see if you can lose some fluid."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 20,
      "time": "2172-02-24 12:34:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Alright. I’ve been having headaches too. Can I take my Imitrex?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 21,
      "time": "2172-02-24 12:35:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Yes, you can take it as prescribed. We’ll keep an eye on it. Also, I see you’re on methadone and Dilaudid for pain. Are you taking them regularly?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 22,
      "time": "2172-02-24 12:36:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Methadone three times a day, and Dilaudid when the pain gets bad. It’s been okay."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 23,
      "time": "2172-02-24 12:37:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "We’ll keep that regimen. Just let us know if you feel too drowsy."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 24,
      "time": "2172-02-24 12:38:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Will do."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 25,
      "time": "2172-02-25 09:00:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Good morning. We did another chest X-ray. The heart looks a bit bigger, and there’s some fluid in the lungs. This confirms your heart failure is flaring up."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 26,
      "time": "2172-02-25 09:01:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Is that serious?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 27,
      "time": "2172-02-25 09:02:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "It’s manageable. We’ll continue the diuretics. You’ve already lost a few pounds—your weight dropped from 424 to 418. That’s a good sign."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 28,
      "time": "2172-02-25 09:03:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Oh, I didn’t even notice. That’s good."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 29,
      "time": "2172-02-25 09:04:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "We also checked for pneumonia, but the consolidation in your lung base isn’t worsening. We don’t think antibiotics are needed yet."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 30,
      "time": "2172-02-25 09:05:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Okay. I’ve been coughing a little, but not too bad."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 31,
      "time": "2172-02-25 09:06:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "We’ll keep monitoring. One more thing—psychiatry spoke with you yesterday. Can we talk about that?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 32,
      "time": "2172-02-25 09:07:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Yeah… I said some things. I’ve been feeling really down. Unsafe at home. It’s been hard."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 33,
      "time": "2172-02-25 09:08:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "I’m sorry you’re going through that. They mentioned you’ve had trauma in the past?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 34,
      "time": "2172-02-25 09:09:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Yes… I was raped ten months ago. I haven’t told many people."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 35,
      "time": "2172-02-25 09:10:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Thank you for sharing that. It takes courage. Psychiatry recommends starting Effexor for depression and anxiety. Would you be open to that?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 36,
      "time": "2172-02-25 09:11:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "I guess so. I need to feel better."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 37,
      "time": "2172-02-25 09:12:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "We’ll start it today. And we’ll connect you with a therapist after discharge."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 38,
      "time": "2172-02-26 10:00:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Your INR is coming down—it’s now 2.9. We’re restarting Coumadin at 10 mg daily."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 39,
      "time": "2172-02-26 10:01:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Is that less than before?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 40,
      "time": "2172-02-26 10:02:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Yes, you were on 11–12 mg alternating. We’re starting lower to avoid another high INR."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 41,
      "time": "2172-02-26 10:03:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Got it."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 42,
      "time": "2172-02-27 09:30:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "You’re doing well. Weight is now 410 lbs. Breathing easier?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 43,
      "time": "2172-02-27 09:31:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Yes, a bit. I can lie flatter now."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 44,
      "time": "2172-02-27 09:32:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Great. We’re going to reduce your Lasix to once daily. If swelling or shortness of breath returns, go back to twice daily."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 45,
      "time": "2172-02-27 09:33:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Okay, I’ll watch for that."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 46,
      "time": "2172-02-28 11:00:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "We did a rib X-ray because of your chest pain. No fracture. It’s likely musculoskeletal."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 47,
      "time": "2172-02-28 11:01:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "It hurts when I press on it. So not my heart?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 48,
      "time": "2172-02-28 11:02:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "No, it doesn’t look like a heart issue. We’ll keep managing it with your pain meds."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 49,
      "time": "2172-02-29 10:15:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Your INR is now 2.4 on 11 mg daily. That’s in the safe range. The rehab facility will manage your Coumadin after discharge."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 50,
      "time": "2172-02-29 10:16:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "So I’m going to rehab?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 51,
      "time": "2172-02-29 10:17:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Yes, to help with mobility and recovery. You’ll continue physical therapy and get support for your mental health too."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 52,
      "time": "2172-02-29 10:18:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Alright. I’m a little nervous, but I’ll try."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 53,
      "time": "2172-03-01 09:45:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Last night’s labs look good. Your kidney function is stable, and your hemoglobin is normal. We’re on track for discharge tomorrow."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 54,
      "time": "2172-03-01 09:46:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "That’s good. What about my HIV and hepatitis?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 55,
      "time": "2172-03-01 09:47:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Both are stable. You stayed on your HIV meds, and your liver enzymes are okay. No changes needed."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 56,
      "time": "2172-03-01 09:48:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Thank you."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 57,
      "time": "2172-03-02 08:00:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Good news—you’re cleared for discharge. You’ll go to rehab, where they’ll help with your fracture recovery and continue your care."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 58,
      "time": "2172-03-02 08:01:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "What about my medications?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 59,
      "time": "2172-03-02 08:02:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "We’ve updated them: Coumadin is now 11 mg daily, Dilaudid is 4 mg every 6 hours as needed, and you’re starting Effexor 150 mg daily. All other meds stay the same."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 60,
      "time": "2172-03-02 08:03:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Okay. I’ll follow up with my doctors after rehab?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 61,
      "time": "2172-03-02 08:04:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Yes—your PCP for blood pressure and INR, and a therapist for mental health. You’re doing great. Take care."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 62,
      "time": "2172-03-02 08:05:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Thank you, Doctor."
    }
  ],
  "summary": {
    "admission_start": "2172-02-24 11:55:00",
    "admission_end": "2172-03-02 13:47:00",
    "summary_paragraph": "The patient was admitted after a mechanical fall from a chair resulting in a left distal tibial fracture. Imaging confirmed the fracture without joint involvement, and orthopedics recommended conservative management. During admission, she was found to have an elevated INR of 7.5 on Coumadin, which was held and later restarted at a reduced dose as it trended down to 2.4. She exhibited signs of acute on chronic diastolic heart failure with volume overload, evidenced by orthopnea, increased leg edema, and radiographic findings; she responded well to diuresis with a weight loss from 424 to 404 pounds. She endorsed passive suicidal ideation and a history of sexual trauma, leading to initiation of Effexor for depression. Her HIV and hepatitis B/C remained stable on treatment. She was discharged to a rehabilitation facility for continued monitoring, physical therapy, and mental health support with updated medication instructions.",
    "problems": [
      "Unspecified fracture of ankle, closed",
      "Acute on chronic diastolic heart failure",
      "Abnormal coagulation profile",
      "Depressive disorder, not elsewhere classified",
      "Asymptomatic human immunodeficiency virus [HIV] infection status",
      "Chronic hepatitis C without mention of hepatic coma",
      "Chronic viral hepatitis B without mention of hepatic coma without mention of hepatitis delta",
      "Personal history of malignant neoplasm of ovary",
      "Morbid obesity",
      "Obstructive sleep apnea (adult)(pediatric)",
      "Other chronic pain",
      "Accidental fall from chair"
    ]
  }
}
